; Two BUILD/EDITOR tools over the one fennec `.mlx` pre-pass (fennec_mlx_prepass). Both are tiny
; wrappers; neither is ever linked into the shipped framework runtime.

; ── fennec-mlx-pp : the dialect PREPROCESSOR (drives the BUILD) ──────────────────────────────────
; Runs the fennec pre-pass, pipes the result through the real mlx-pp, and rewrites the embedded
; source filename back to the original .mlx path. Installed with a public_name so the workspace
; dialect's (preprocess (run fennec-mlx-pp …)) can invoke it by bare name (like mlx-pp from PATH).
; Depends on compiler-libs (Parsetree/Ast_mapper/Config) only to swap the filename in mlx-pp's binary
; AST — a value-level rewrite, robust to marshalling layout.

(executable
 (name fennec_mlx_pp)
 (public_name fennec-mlx-pp)
 (package fennec-cli)
 (modules fennec_mlx_pp)
 (libraries fennec_mlx_prepass unix compiler-libs.common))

; ── ocamlmerlin-fennec-mlx : the dialect MERLIN READER (fixes the EDITOR) ────────────────────────
; The dialect's (merlin_reader fennec-mlx) makes Merlin spawn `ocamlmerlin-fennec-mlx` as the
; external reader for .mlx buffers in the EDITOR. It runs the SAME pre-pass over the editor buffer,
; then DELEGATES to the stock `ocamlmerlin-mlx` reader (spawned as a child via merlin-extend's
; Extend_driver) on the transformed buffer — so bare-text .mlx stops showing false in-editor syntax
; errors while hover / complete / jump keep working (the pre-pass is line-preserving, so positions are
; line-exact; only columns inside a quoted prose run shift).
;
; merlin-extend is an EDITOR-only dependency that ships with merlin / ocaml-lsp-server. To guarantee
; the BUILD never depends on merlin, the reader body is a `(select)` over it: when merlin-extend is
; present dune compiles fennec_mlx_reader.real.ml (the real reader); when ABSENT it compiles
; fennec_mlx_reader.stub.ml (a build-only stub), so `dune build @all` / @check stay green with no
; merlin in the environment. (An (optional) executable does NOT achieve this — dune still tries to
; build it under @all and fails when the library is missing; only a select cleanly substitutes.)
; compiler-libs.common precedes the select so it links before merlin-extend (which depends on Config);
; the public_name is exactly the binary name Merlin looks for on PATH (ocamlmerlin-<reader-name>).

(executable
 (name ocamlmerlin_fennec_mlx)
 (public_name ocamlmerlin-fennec-mlx)
 (package fennec-cli)
 (modules ocamlmerlin_fennec_mlx fennec_mlx_reader)
 (libraries
  fennec_mlx_prepass
  compiler-libs.common
  (select fennec_mlx_reader.ml from
   (merlin-extend -> fennec_mlx_reader.real.ml)
   (-> fennec_mlx_reader.stub.ml))))
